### 3.3 `src/components/WebGPUCanvas.tsx` - Expand Minimum Octave Range So Piano Roll Fills Full Vertical Height

In `src/components/WebGPUCanvas.tsx`, inside the `useMemo` that computes `{ minMidi, maxMidi, maxEndWhole }`:

1. When `!visibleEvents || visibleEvents.length === 0`, return `{ minMidi: 36, maxMidi: 84, maxEndWhole: 4 }` (4 full octaves from `C2` to `C6`).
2. Increase `pad` and `minSpan` so single-note sketches always display at least 36 semitones (3 full octaves, `minSpan = selectedTrackId ? 28 : 36`, `pad = 12`) centered around the active notes, filling the vertical height of the right pane:

```typescript
    const centerMidi = Math.round((min + max) / 2);
    const minSpan = selectedTrackId ? 28 : 36;
    const halfSpan = Math.max(Math.ceil((max - min) / 2) + 6, Math.floor(minSpan / 2));
    const paddedMin = Math.max(12, centerMidi - halfSpan);
    const paddedMax = Math.min(108, Math.max(paddedMin + minSpan, centerMidi + halfSpan));
    return {
      minMidi: paddedMin,
      maxMidi: paddedMax,
      maxEndWhole: Math.max(4, maxWhole),
    };

```

